WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:16.587
one week after Heidi started praying, the tutor asked to speak with Clara's grandmother.

2
00:00:17.648 --> 00:00:20.130
He wanted to tell her about something remarkable.

3
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:25.073
"Something I had stopped hoping for has happened," said the tutor.

4
00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:28.356
"It can only be looked upon as a miracle."

5
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:32.565
"Has Heidi learned to read at last?"

6
00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:33.926
asked Grandmamma.

7
00:00:34.946 --> 00:00:37.127
The tutor looked at the lady with astonishment.

8
00:00:37.147 --> 00:00:38.888
"How did you guess?"

9
00:00:39.268 --> 00:00:39.748
he asked.

10
00:00:39.768 --> 00:00:42.009
"It is truly marvelous!

11
00:00:43.029 --> 00:00:45.490
At first she seemed unable to learn her letters.

12
00:00:46.371 --> 00:00:48.892
Now it is as if she has learned them overnight."

13
00:00:48.912 --> 00:00:56.275
"Many unlikely things happen in life," said Grandmamma with a pleased smile.

14
00:00:57.155 --> 00:01:01.325
Grandmamma was so pleased that she wanted to reward Heidi with a present.

15
00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.966
She found her reading aloud to Clara.

16
00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:08.968
"Heidi, I am so pleased that you have learned to read.

17
00:01:09.928 --> 00:01:13.550
The picture book is yours to keep," Grandmamma said.

18
00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.371
Heidi was overwhelmed with delight.

19
00:01:17.391 --> 00:01:20.092
"Mine to keep always?

20
00:01:20.773 --> 00:01:22.073
Even when I go home?"

21
00:01:22.673 --> 00:01:24.374
said Heidi, blushing with pleasure.

22
00:01:24.394 --> 00:01:30.405
"Yes, of course, yours forever," Grandmamma assured her.

23
00:01:32.205 --> 00:01:36.907
When Heidi went to bed that night, she looked at her book again before falling asleep.

24
00:01:37.788 --> 00:01:44.710
From that day forward, her chief pleasure was to read over and over again the tales that belonged

25
00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.052
to the beautiful pictures of the shepherd and his flock.

26
00:01:49.732 --> 00:01:54.254
Heidi often went to Grandmamma's room in the afternoons while Clara took her nap.

27
00:01:55.074 --> 00:01:58.756
There she learned to sew, and Grandmamma listened to Heidi read aloud.

28
00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:02.557
All the people Heidi read about became like dear friends.

29
00:02:03.377 --> 00:02:05.138
It always delighted her to be with them.

30
00:02:05.878 --> 00:02:08.158
But Heidi's homesickness never left her.

31
00:02:09.919 --> 00:02:14.900
In the last week of her visit, Grandmamma called Heidi into her room one evening after dinner.

32
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.662
"Now, child," she said, "tell me why you are not happy?

33
00:02:20.682 --> 00:02:24.703
Do you still have the same trouble in your heart?"

34
00:02:26.264 --> 00:02:27.664
Heidi nodded in reply.

35
00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.449
"Have you told God about it?"

36
00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.532
"Yes," said Heidi, sadly.

37
00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:40.036
"And do you pray every night to ask God to make things right so that you may be

38
00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:40.856
happy again?"

39
00:02:40.877 --> 00:02:45.840
"No, I have stopped praying," said Heidi.

40
00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.282
Grandmamma was surprised.

41
00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:51.464
"Do not tell me that!

42
00:02:52.324 --> 00:02:54.165
Why have you stopped praying?"

43
00:02:54.185 --> 00:02:57.568
"It doesn't do any good.

44
00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.381
God does not listen," Heidi said in an agitated voice.

45
00:03:02.401 --> 00:03:07.763
"How can He listen when so many people pray to Him every night?

46
00:03:08.643 --> 00:03:10.123
He cannot hear them all.

47
00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:13.644
He certainly has not heard what I said to Him."

48
00:03:13.664 --> 00:03:16.705
"You are wrong, Heidi.

49
00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:19.846
You must not think of Him like that.

50
00:03:20.887 --> 00:03:22.087
God has heard you.

51
00:03:22.707 --> 00:03:27.933
If He has not given you what you prayed for, He will give you something better when the

52
00:03:28.013 --> 00:03:28.893
time is right.

53
00:03:29.993 --> 00:03:32.714
He knows better than we do what is good for us.

54
00:03:33.694 --> 00:03:36.275
Continue to pray and to trust Him."

55
00:03:37.776 --> 00:03:43.337
Heidi had perfect confidence in Grandmamma, and every word she said sank into her heart.

56
00:03:44.337 --> 00:03:49.159
That night, Heidi prayed once again so that God would go on thinking about her.

57
00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:52.840
The day came for Grandmamma to leave.

58
00:03:53.716 --> 00:04:01.080
Both Clara and Heidi were very sad, but all morning, Grandmamma kept them lively and amused with songs

59
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.202
and games so that they had no time to be unhappy.

60
00:04:05.763 --> 00:04:08.685
After she had left, the house seemed silent and empty.

61
00:04:09.605 --> 00:04:13.628
Clara and Heidi sat the remainder of the day like two lost children.
